The standard way to attribute a quotation puts a footer inside the quote:

> Simplicity is prerequisite for reliability.
> 
> — Edsger W. Dijkstra

![a punch card](https://example.com/images/punch-card.jpg)

A program, before version control.

Both the attribution and the caption belong to the post.
